Z||000026||DRH||08-25-2001||10:15 PM||||Ours just hit 1.799 for regualar. It's gone up about .25 in the last week (.15 last Wednesday) and about .40 since it's low about a month ago.<P>There was an article in the paper about a Citgo refinery having a fire in IL. They said that was making the supply tighter and forcing the price up. If the supply is short, why have I NEVER seen a station run out of even a particular grade?<P>I think this is the latest  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> excuse to run prices up just in time for Labor Day.<P>||||reg||1
