Z||000032||86seyellow||08-26-2001||07:39 PM||||$1.79 87 octane. 2 weeks ago was 1.39. I think it is trying to get all they can for the last holiday. Businsess is slow and they are trying to make up for it. One station told me 2 refineries shut down. I dont believe it. GAs isnt tight supply. If it was we would all be limited like the 70s. Im to young for that but I remeber the articles<P>All the gas stations price fix in there area. I know in LAcrosse wiasonsin , they have a meeting on sat morning and lal the stations agree to one price. They say it isnt fixing but determining profits<BR><P>------------------<BR>if you saw a yellow streak go by you really fast it was a fiero<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
