Z||000038||mrfiero||08-27-2001||03:09 AM||||It's between 1.45-$1.59 for regular here in Brighton.  We were less than $1.30 just a little over a week ago. <P>When I returned from my California trip it was $1.24.  I went to fill up the next day and it was $1.39!  It jumped 15 cents overnight.  The price just jumped again.....now the same station is $1.49.<P>No matter what excuse (refinery fire, etc.) it's just that, an excuse.  Labor day is upon us and the oil companies want to boost their bottom line.  It sucks, but that's what we get for having a free market.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BTW.......it'll go up again, so fill up now.  I'm guessing there's another 10-15 cents to go before it starts to drop again. <BR>     ||||reg||1
